Sorry for you inconvenience. My question was following :

Theory says according to Drule choose that item which satisfies following condition, attached in fig1 (first figure).
which contains determinant of sum of both test information till k-1 item and item information for kth item.

According to the code in Drule it says

crit <- lapply(infos, function(x, person) det(x + person$info_thetas), person=person)

Here, determinant function is applied over infos  using lapply function. Infos are only the item information. and person$info_thetas are always zero.

So in the code are we only doing as shown in fig2 (second figure) ?

And the reason behind doing so is following inequality?

det(A+B)≥detA+detB

