I'm not sure what you mean. The last category in a Likert is most difficult by definition since all categories are ordered.

>
> 2.035
>
> 0.272
>
> -0.78
>
> -1.81
>
> -2.93
>
> -4.6
> And i Mean by question "can we use regression or correlation between scores in order to test our Hypothesis?" that when we use "coef(mod1)"  in MIRT package it gives us ability or trait ( ).

No, coef returns the item parameters. It has nothing to do with theta estimates.

> can we use regression or correlations between  in order to test our hypothesis?

You can, but you shouldn't. You'll experience shrinkage effects due to factor score prediction. The better way to do this is via latent regression methods, but they are currently only available on the development version (or if you are using Rasch models, this is possible in mixedmirt already).

Phil

